  "title": "Yang et al. 2025 — A multi-day and high-quality EEG dataset for motor imagery brain-computer interface",
  "description": "A multi-day EEG dataset for motor imagery brain-computer interface (MI-BCI) research collected at Shanghai University (WBCIC-SHU). It contains recordings from 51 healthy, BCI-naive participants who performed left- and right-hand motor imagery over three sessions on different days. A subset of 11 participants also performed a three-class paradigm that adds foot-hooking imagery. Recordings were made with a 59-channel EEG system and the dataset is accompanied by benchmark classification results using CSP, FBCSP, EEGNet, deepConvNet and FBCNet.",
  "methods_description": "EEG was recorded at 1000 Hz with a Neuracle NeuSen W system using Ag/AgCl electrodes (59 EEG channels plus ECG and EOG channels). Participants followed video cues in trials of 7.5 s, with a 1.5 s cue and 4 s of motor imagery. Each participant completed 3 sessions on different days, with 200 trials per session in the two-class task and 300 in the three-class task, without feedback (offline). Benchmark classification used 10-fold within-session cross-validation.",
